  "title": "Pin Rust 1.99.0 in CI and tighten empty-collection assertions",
  "summary": "The CI workflow stops adding clippy/rustfmt to whatever toolchain the dev container happens to ship and instead installs a pinned Rust 1.99.0 with those components, then makes it the default. Alongside that, the test suites across osf-lint-core and osf replace `assert!(x.is_empty())` with `assert_eq!(x, Vec::<T>::new())` so a failure prints the offending contents instead of a bare boolean. No production logic changes: the lint rules, config loader, reviewer roster, work-item parser and moon report parser behave exactly as before.",
